/// @title Book
/// @notice Current per-pool storage: tick bitmap, priority tree and exact-price summaries.
/// @dev A pool's state hangs off P = keccak(poolId, POOLS_SEED):
///      P + 0: nextSequence (bits 0–63) | openOrderCount (64–127).
///      P + 3: order mapping; P + 4: maker/executor mapping; P + 5/6: bid/ask levels.
///      P + 7: initialized; P + 16..18/19..21: bid/ask tick bitmap hierarchy.
///      P + 23/24/25: quote minimum, asset minimum, priority cap; P + 26/27: reference tick/block.
///      P + 1/2 and the old ordering-mode bits are reserved legacy layout space.
///
///      Seven-slot order O: packed owner/isBuy/zeroForOne/escrowed/priorityFee at O + 0;
///      price128 | priorityKey128 at O + 1; amountIn/minimum at O + 2/3;
///      original maker sequence at O + 4; reprices at O + 5; queue sequence at O + 6.
///      Maker age survives fee top-ups; queue age changes when a bid rejoins its level.
///
///      Level L: L + 2 count, L + 3 priority radix tree, L + 4 priorityKey-to-order mapping,
///      L + 5 exact-price subtree summaries (two words per node). L + 0/1 are reserved.
///      Exact ratios outrank bids; bid and queue sequence break exact-price ties.

